    "description": "Friday evening vault lint — structural health check",
    "prompt": "Pull the vault and run the lint workflow. Report orphan pages, unresolved links, and index gaps. Keep it to the top 5 issues ranked by severity.",
    "skill": "obsidian-vault",
    "platform": "whatsapp"
  },
  {
    "name": "meeting-briefing",
    "schedule": "*/15 7-19 * * 1-5",
    "description": "Meeting briefing — context prep for meetings starting in 30-45 minutes",
    "prompt": "Pull the vault. Use the google MCP (listEvents tool) to check for calendar events starting in 30 to 45 minutes. Skip all-day events, solo blocks, and events titled Focus, Block, Lunch, Commute, Personal, OOO, or Out of Office. For each qualifying meeting, gather attendee context from vault people notes, check Linear for related issues, search recent emails with attendees via listMessages, search the vault for previous meeting notes and action items. Create or update a meeting note in the vault at /vault/calendar/meetings/ with full context, then commit and push. Deliver a concise plain-text briefing via WhatsApp with meeting details, relevant context, and anything that needs attention. If no meetings qualify, produce no output at all.",
    "skill": "meeting-briefing",
    "platform": "whatsapp"
  },
  {
    "name": "email-draft-replies",
    "schedule": "0 19 * * 1-5",
    "description": "Draft suggested replies for emails that need a response",
    "prompt": "Use listMessages to find emails received today that look like they need a reply from me — direct questions, requests, or action items. Skip newsletters, notifications, and automated messages. For each email needing a reply, use createDraft to draft a concise, professional response. After drafting, send me a brief summary of what was drafted and for whom. If nothing needs a reply, produce no output at all.",
    "platform": "whatsapp"
  }
